<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <!--
        DISPLAY LABEL. masterLabel is what an admin reads in the Lightning App Builder palette, so it
        tracks the card title, which has carried four names: "Same Email" to "Portfolio Deal"
        (retracted) to "Property Package" and now back to "Portfolio Deal" - the underlying object's
        own label. Entry 2 was retracted at the time because it collided with a live Opportunity stage
        value of that name; that value and the three Opportunity fields behind it were retired in
        phases A1-A3 of the Portfolio Deal rename, so the wording is now correct rather than banned.

        THE BUNDLE'S API NAME IS `portfolioDealSiblings`, RENAMED FROM `packageSiblings` IN PHASE B4
        of that same program. An LWC bundle rename is a delete and create and it DOES break any page
        that binds the old API name, so Lead_Record_Page and Opportunity_Record_Page were re-pointed
        in the same wave; a page still naming `packageSiblings` renders nothing, silently.
    -->
    <masterLabel>Portfolio Deal</masterLabel>
    <description>Other Leads and Opportunities created from the same multi-property broker email. One object-agnostic bundle for both the Lead and Opportunity record pages; renders nothing when the record has no Portfolio Deal.</description>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__RecordPage</target>
    </targets>
</LightningComponentBundle>
